{
  "title": "koylu_muhabbet_nogay",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "node:start",
      "type": "START",
      "position": "(0.0, 0.0)"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:selam",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(350.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Nogay",
      "text": "Quiet, gatekeeper... When the wind blows from the crags, the scent of the soil shifts. I track footprints along the forest border."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_normal",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, -180.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "Nogay, what tracks have you observed along the mountain paths and perimeter fence?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_kriz",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "Were you able to find the tracks of the raiders who lit campfires in the pine woods?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:opt_karar",
      "type": "DIALOGUE_OPTION",
      "position": "(700.0, 180.0)",
      "character": "Gatekeeper",
      "text": "What do the trail tracks reveal about the scouts and shepherds we admitted?"
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_normal",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, -180.0)",
      "character": "Nogay",
      "text": "The wolf tracks wild goats, while human tracks seek the smoke of the village chimney. For now the border is quiet, yet I never take my eye from the pine boughs. Tracks never tell falsehoods."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_kriz",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, 0.0)",
      "character": "Nogay",
      "text": "They were scouts from the Red Crow outlaw band... Three horsemen descended into the valley and surveyed the village gate. I tracked their trail down to the river shingle. I laid snare pits; whoever approaches will tumble into the trap."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:rep_karar",
      "type": "DIALOGUE",
      "position": "(1050.0, 180.0)",
      "character": "Nogay",
      "text": "I examined the tracks of the shepherd with the lame kid by the creek; his flight from the outlaws was genuine. The mountain passes described by the tower trumpeter match the hoofprints perfectly. You admitted the right men."
    },
    {
      "id": "node:act_normal",
      "type": "ACTION",
      "position": "(1400.0, -180.0)",
      "description": "Köy Morali",
      "action_type": "SCRIPT",
      "action_script_ref": "res://src/diyalog/actions/koy_moral_action.gd",
      "values": [
        "2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "node:act_kriz",
      "type": "ACTION",
      "position": "(1400.0, 0.0)",
      "description": "Köy Morali",
      "action_type": "SCRIPT",
